CDNCA client_max_body_size with variables.  Original CDNCA change, not
upstream.  With one shared server{} per port (docs/adr/0009, 1.0.36) the
upload limit must follow the site chosen at request time, and a Lua
Content-Length check cannot see chunked HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2 or HTTP/3 bodies.
A value with variables is evaluated once per request body; empty,
malformed, zero or overflowing values reject the request with 500 instead
of lifting the limit.  A value without variables keeps the stock semantics.

